## 7. Migration Execution Plan

### Step-by-Step

| Step | Action | Who | Verify |
|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | Create full database backup | DBA | Backup file exists |
| 2 | Note v1.0 record counts | DBA | Counts documented |
| 3 | Test v1.0 Edge Functions | Developer | All 3 functions work |
| 4 | Run `005_v2_schema.sql` | DBA | New tables created |
| 5 | Run `008_v2_migration.sql` | DBA | Data migrated |
| 6 | Run validation queries | DBA | All checks pass |
| 7 | Run `006_v2_security.sql` | DBA | RLS applied |
| 8 | Run `007_v2_functions.sql` | DBA | Functions created |
| 9 | Run `009_v2_seed.sql` | DBA | Test data added |
| 10 | Run `010_v2_storage.sql` | DBA | Storage buckets ready |
| 11 | Test v1.0 Edge Functions again | Developer | Still operational |
| 12 | Deploy v2.0 Edge Functions | Developer | New functions work |
| 13 | Test v2.0 iOS app | Developer | All flows work |

### Rollback Trigger
If ANY of these occur, execute rollback:
- Data loss detected (record counts mismatch)
- v1.0 Edge Functions broken
- Critical RLS policy failure
- Financial totals mismatch

